@startuml
title Task 6: daily local index update
actor User
node "Windows Task Scheduler\n18:00 daily; missed-run catch-up" as Scheduler
folder "task-6/incoming/\neditable local source" as Source
component "update_index.py\nlock + hashes + change detection" as Updater
component "task-3 chunk_document\n100-300 words" as Splitter
component "Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B\nsame pinned revision" as Encoder
database "task-6/index/snapshot.zip\nFAISS + chunks + manifest" as Index
file "task-6/logs/updates.jsonl" as Logs
component "task-6/bot.py\nreload between requests" as Bot
User --> Source : add / edit / remove
Scheduler --> Updater : project Python
Source --> Updater : scan + read locally
Index --> Updater : reuse unchanged vectors
Updater --> Splitter
Splitter --> Encoder : only uncached chunk texts
Encoder --> Updater : normalized vectors
Updater --> Index : validate temporary ZIP, atomic replace
Updater --> Logs : times, counts, size, errors
Index --> Bot : consistent snapshot
note right of Updater
Failure: old snapshot stays usable.
Scheduler retries twice.
No Ollama call during indexing.
end note
@enduml
